menu "Rover firmware"

    config ROVER_DEBUG_BUILD
        bool "Debug build (console and logging enabled)"
        default n
        help
            A37: the debug console is build-time and off in release. A release
            build sets CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_NONE and has no console on
            USB-Serial/JTAG, on the CP2102 UART0 bridge, or on UART1 -- a live
            text path into the motor controller is a second writer bypassing
            session, seq and CRC (I-18).

            Enabling this only advertises the fact: it sets caps bit 0 and
            ctrl_flags b7 in the boot banner, so the Pi can see which kind of
            build it is talking to and refuse to arm a debug build. Build with
            sdkconfig.defaults.debug to also turn the console back on.

endmenu
